  source_path scripts/build-actor-graph.mjs
  source_path scripts/build_actor_graph.py.archive
  witness scripts/tests/build-actor-graph.test.mjs proves source-bound identities remain distinct for equal bylines and all generated actor observations stay asserted
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/people_projection.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreActors/tests/organ_callers_test.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/people_projection_test.c
  witness engine/core/tests/actor_graph_test.c
  witness cmd/BonfyreActors/tests/organ_callers_test.sh proves asserted actor records, typed edges and distinct-source corroboration flow through the native caller; repeating a source does not increase the independent count
  witness 2026-09-24 the current 68,944-item estate replayed 6,452 source-bound asserted name observations (4,441 person-shaped and 2,011 publication-shaped) into the native ActorGraph; equal names across sources remain separate actor coordinates and no cross-source name string was promoted or counted as corroboration
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/people_projection_test.c proves the public directory links each (source, by) credit to its own profile host, an exact source surface cannot cross the source boundary, and a legacy name-only address offers source choices rather than asserting identity
  source_lineage capitalgym crm relationships
  known_gap native writer records actors/edges on the shared store with the declared-kind, mandatory-provenance and non-collapsing-confidence gates (python reads native-written rows, tier preserved -- proven); native corroboration/verification-profile promotion logic is the remaining native-absorption item
  known_gap the former name-collapsed 2,143-row derived ActorGraph is retained locally as actors-legacy-name-collapsed-20260924T163000Z.db for recovery; it must not be consumed as identity truth because its key omitted the asserting source

  known_gap the Python peer's witness for this organ no longer exists on disk; the entry named a file that could not be opened, which is the one thing a witness must never be. The line is removed rather than repointed, and the live evidence for this architecture is what remains listed.
  known_gap the native caller is an explicit operator CLI, not yet a standing archive-to-actor ingestion pass; a credited byline remains asserted until an operator supplies its provenance and no name is auto-merged into an identity.
  interacts web-address-edge
architecture role-program-compiler
  canonical_name RoleProgramCompiler
  family identity
  domain Identity / Operating posture
  layer compiler
  semantic_question How can one Actor assume distinct modern operating responsibilities over shared subjects without becoming a different Actor kind or receiving portable authority?
  purpose Compiles declared role programs into CMS-native operating postures: subject and relationship neighborhoods, public search reach, CRM lenses, work queues, capability references, exact existing Foundry operations, metric views, handoff contracts and a SurfaceScene preference. It compiles requested operations only when FoundryBehaviorCompiler already emitted their exact contract; every other requested verb remains explicit unresolved work. A signed-in actor may assume a published program in an explicit context scope through the native RoleAssignment owner and read only their own compiled Operator Passport workspace. The assignment is a posture, not an authority grant.
  maturity implemented
  owns RoleProgram
  owns RoleAssignment
  consumes Actor
  consumes ExactObjectContractCatalog
  consumes CapabilityProgram
  consumes SurfaceScene
  publishes RoleProgramCatalog
  node_types RoleProgram
  node_types RoleAssignment
  edge_types assumes_operating_posture
  edge_types selects_lens
  invariant a role program composes shared Actor, subject, relationship, CRM, WorkGraph, capability and authority substrates; it never creates an occupational Actor subtype
  invariant global role reach is restricted to declared public search scopes while every effect remains checked by its native authority owner in the local subject context
  invariant requested role operations absent from the exact Foundry catalog remain unresolved and do not become a surface aperture or an ObjectContract
  invariant a RoleAssignment names one signed-in actor, one published RoleProgram and one explicit scope, and is replay-safe per actor/program/scope; a second scope cannot overwrite the first and a failed native write cannot be reported as an assumed role
  forbidden_inference a RoleAssignment -> authority grant, provider access, institutional role, employment relationship, representation right, or permission to act
  forbidden_inference a RoleProgram's global public reach -> global effect authority
  source_path schemas/control/role-program-specs.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/tools/compile_role_program.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/tools/compile_role_program.py.archive
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/role_program.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/role_assignment.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  witness cmd/BonfyreCMS/tools/compile_role_program.test.mjs proves Brand Operator, Go-to-Market Engineer and Internet Operator compile to real RoleProgram rows; only existing exact Foundry operations emit and requested ownerless role verbs remain unresolved
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/role_program_owner_test.sh proves one actor can retain two separate scopes of the same published operating program and read each private workspace without granting either to another actor
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/role_program_owner_test.sh proves an authenticated actor can assume Internet Operator in one community scope, then reads only their own private Operator Passport workspace with compiled lenses, queues, exact operations and authority requirements; anonymous and cross-actor reads are refused and the stored assignment cannot infer an authority grant
  known_gap the private Operator Passport is a native JSON workspace; a richer interactive SurfaceScene is not yet rendered over it
  known_gap local authority remains separately checked per native effect owner; no role program presently carries a proof-backed authority grant workflow

interaction role-program-compiler-uses-foundry-contracts
  source role-program-compiler
  destination foundry-behavior-compiler
  relation filters_to_exact_operations
  preserves only an exact target kind and verified native owner operation already emitted by the Foundry compiler
  drops every requested operation lacking a verified owner, along with any implied authority or effect
  forbidden_inference a role-requested operation -> an emitted ObjectContract or a usable action
  invalidates_on role spec, Foundry catalog, exact operation target, or native owner changing
  binding cmd/BonfyreCMS/tools/compile_role_program.mjs
  witness cmd/BonfyreCMS/tools/compile_role_program.test.mjs

architecture verification-ledger
  canonical_name VerificationLedger
  owns Corroboration
  consumes Actor
  consumes FortificationPlan
  publishes Corroboration
  publishes Actor
  family identity
  domain Identity / Institutional Capacity
  layer identity
  semantic_question Is this actor independently corroborated enough to promote asserted -> verified?
  purpose The gated mechanism a fortification "verify" action executes against. Records corroborations (actor, source, evidence) and promotes asserted -> verified only at a threshold of INDEPENDENT sources, never on the actor's own say-so. Closes the feedback loop: a load-bearing asserted actor is a fortification target; once independently corroborated and promoted, it drops off the CollapseFront verify plan -- risk actually retired, not merely noted.
  maturity measured
  node_types Corroboration
  edge_types corroborates
  state_types asserted
  state_types verified
  internal_calculus distinct-source count gate; monotone promotion at threshold k (default 2)
  invariant independence is by distinct source; a repeated source is one corroboration, so an actor cannot bootstrap its own verification
  invariant promotion is monotone -- never demotes, never promotes below threshold
  invariant promotion writes back through actors.upsert_actor, so the confidence change is a normal graph write, not a side channel
  forbidden_inference a corroboration was recorded -> the actor is verified (below threshold it stays asserted)
  forbidden_inference promoted to verified -> the claim is true (independently attested is not proven)
  interacts actor-graph
  interacts collapse-front
  interacts fortification-plan
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/verification.py.archive
  source_path engine/core/src/corroboration.c
  source_path engine/core/include/bf_corroboration.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreActors/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreActors/tests/organ_callers_test.sh
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_verification.py.archive
  witness engine/core/tests/corroboration_test.c
  witness cmd/BonfyreActors/tests/organ_callers_test.sh proves the native caller records only distinct corroborating sources and returns repeat-source rather than inflating the count
  source_lineage fortification verify action needs a real gated mechanism
  known_gap native ledger records corroborations on the shared actor_corroborations store with distinct-source independence (python reads native-written rows -- parity proven); the promotion gate stays python/human (native never promotes -- the human line)

architecture hash-identity
  canonical_name HashIdentityGraph
  family identity
  domain Identity
  layer identity
  semantic_question Are these byte/content objects identical?
  purpose Content-addressed identity: bytes -> digest -> Merkle membership. Used by artifacts, packs, model weights, receipts.
  maturity implemented
  node_types ContentObject
  edge_types hashes_to
  edge_types merkle_member_of
  forbidden_inference same bytes -> same derivational meaning
  native_format graf
  command BonfyreHash
  source_path cmd/BonfyreHash
  source_lineage identity federation seed

architecture estate-identity-graph
  canonical_name EstateIdentityGraph
  family identity
  domain Identity / What the estate's material names
  layer store
  semantic_question When this estate's sources keep saying a name, what is the thing, and how does a composed page come to know it?
  purpose The names this estate's material repeats, resolved to identities in the native identity organ: an entity per thing, an observation per fact about it, a link per pair the material names together. Composed pages read it where they are composed.
  maturity implemented
  node_types Entity
  node_types Observation
  node_types EntityLink
  edge_types observed_as
  edge_types named_together_with
  internal_calculus an identity is an entity and its observations, not a row. The register's identifier, the description and the coordinate are observations *about* one entity, each carrying the source that made it and how sure that source was, so a reader can see who claimed what
  internal_calculus a name of two or more words is admitted readily; almost nothing says "Fort Worth" by accident. A single word must resolve to an instance rather than a class, and to something the world carries heavily, or it is refused
  internal_calculus the longest name that fits wins, enforced rather than merely ordered for, and word boundaries include punctuation
  invariant an observation about an entity that does not exist is refused rather than allowed to invent the entity it would describe
  forbidden_inference a title naming an entity -> the piece being about that entity; mention is not aboutness
  forbidden_inference two entities named in one title -> a relationship between them; it is co-mention, and the link says so
  forbidden_inference a resolved identity -> the right one for this corpus; a bare label resolves to what the register labels that way, so Apple is a fruit and Amazon a river
  source_path cmd/BonfyreEntity/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path scripts/resolve-entities.mjs
  source_path scripts/entity-resolution.cue
  source_path scripts/resolve_entities.py.archive
  witness scripts/tests/resolve_entities.test.mjs proves the native resolver extracts actual repeated names from retained Parquet, refuses ordinary English, classes and thin single-word names, selects the most-linked Q identity, attaches only returned coordinates, stages with its CUE policy, preserves the prior complete cut on provider refusal and never promotes mention into aboutness; live QLever execution is not part of the fixture
  witness 2026-09-25 the organ could create an entity from an observation but had no way to attach a second observation to an existing one, so an identifier and a coordinate about one thing minted two entities; `observe` was written in C, and `resolve` now fills the source column it had declared and never written
  witness 2026-09-25 519 entities and 1,660 observations built through the organ, 300 links from co-mention, with 124 candidates refused as ordinary English, 558 as a class rather than a thing of that class, and 49 as too thinly linked to be what a headline meant
  witness 2026-09-25 served by the estate's own C server: the item page for Fort Worth names Fort Worth alone, and a photograph captioned in Fort Worth, Texas names both -- after the match was fixed to treat punctuation as a boundary and to suppress a name contained in a longer accepted one, which had been reporting a German municipality called Worth
  known_gap resolution is by label, so an entity whose label differs from the name a headline uses is missed, and a bare surname resolves to whoever the register labels that way
  known_gap the links record co-mention only; nothing distinguishes two things being discussed together from two things being related
  known_gap the native resolver has deterministic Parquet and mocked-QLever witnesses but has not replayed the live catalog or verified the external endpoint response after cutover
  interacts identity-graph-reaches-composed-pages

interaction identity-graph-reaches-composed-pages
  source estate-identity-graph
  destination page-composition
  relation reads_from
  preserves the composer as the only thing that decides what a page says; the graph supplies identities and never material
  drops any path by which reading an identity could write one, or by which a page could admit an entity
  forbidden_inference an identity shown beneath a piece -> the piece being about it
  witness 2026-09-25 page_emit_entities reads the identity graph read-only at compose time and renders what it observed with each observation's source; the twelve page tests pass unchanged
  binding cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  binding cmd/BonfyreEntity/src/main.c
